  "step_3": "The decision reason requires comparing the mean differences from a reference value (zero) weighted by probabilities. In this case, both lotteries have the same expected value: -6 euros. Thus, the mean difference is identical, and the reason would be indifferent. However, the individual does not mention the reference value, nor does the individual calculate or refer to the expected differences or mean differences. Instead, the justification is based solely on the absolute size of the loss (3000 vs. 6000 euros) and its psychological impact, not on a weighted difference from a reference. Therefore, the individual did not apply the decision reason — they used a different criterion (absolute loss size and perceived psychological impact). The information considered by the individual (absolute loss) is not equivalent to the information required by the decision reason (mean differences from reference value weighted by probabilities). The justification does not reflect the rule of the decision reason. Hence, the decision reason was not used.",
